      "side": 0,
      "message": "this was always a limitation of the existing API. While internally we only support encoders and decoders, this should be more like a mode, such as AMediaCodecKind AMediaCodecInfo_getKind(const AMediaCodecInfo* _NonNull info) - we use Kind in C2 terminology for this.\n\nThen we could have it return\n\nAMediaCodecKind_ENCODER\nor _DECODER\nor _INVALID for the case where info is invalid.\n\nWill we validate the info parameter? E.g. whether it was returned from a call, or do we require it to be a returned value? We could check against NULL, but this return value suggests that we are doing some sort of verification beyond null-ness, which will add to the cost. In most other cases we assume that these pointers are returned from our call and are therefore valid.\n\nSince this parameter is marked non-null, it is also considered bad practice to check for nullness, which further reduces the need for an invalid value.",
